From workstream 05, for workstream 04 to integrate (shared core).

- CitizenLanes: every action of an owner's agents (one Citizen, one
  session key) runs build -> sign -> send one at a time, in arrival
  order, in this relay process; a failure frees the lane; other
  Citizens are not held up. submit queues #run on laneOf(rec); the gate
  and the hold still run synchronously when the turn comes; a replay of
  a remembered key does not queue.
- A Duplicate of a seq action (SendCaravan) is answered as failed with
  sent: null and the earlier transaction's signature (the relay's
  Duplicate carries it) and lifetime: the same bytes already left, so it
  is followed by fate and held while unknown, never read as not-sent.
  This request's own hold is released (it sent nothing itself).

Not covered: other relay processes or machines (the lane is in-process).

Test agent-wallet-citizen-lane (no key made or used, nothing signed):
3 pass; with sender-capability and run-facts: 10 pass.
